@startuml dat-traditional-node
' ============================================================================
' dat-traditional-node.puml — the pointer-based trie node DAT replaces.
' Replaces the ASCII node record in docs/algorithms/implementations/double-array-trie.md.
' Drawn as a CONTIGUOUS colored field table (field + size columns) hosted in a
' floating note; rows share borders (no gaps). Full-cell color via Creole |<#hex>|
' cells. The overhead problems are preserved as a text block below the table.
' Color key:  red #FFCDD2  the costly traditional node (high overhead, pointer chasing)
' ============================================================================
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam TitleFontSize 15
skinparam noteFontSize 14
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #37474F
}

title Traditional trie node (32–64 bytes)

note as TR
|= field |= size |
|<#FFCDD2> is_final |<#FFCDD2> 1 byte |
|<#FFCDD2> children : HashMap / Vec |<#FFCDD2> 24–56 bytes · pointer-chased |

Problems: high per-node overhead · pointer chasing (cache misses) ·
unpredictable memory-access patterns
end note

legend bottom
| Color | Field |
|<#FFCDD2>| costly traditional node (high overhead, pointer chasing) |
endlegend
@enduml
